# One line ending everywhere.
#
# The apps' runtime version is a fingerprint, and the fingerprint hashes the
# CONTENTS of files such as eas.json, google-services.json and the config
# plugins. On Windows git checks files out with CRLF (core.autocrlf), on the
# build servers and in CI they are LF - and a single differing byte gives a
# different hash, so an over-the-air update would be published for a runtime
# that no installed build has. Forcing LF makes the hash the same everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
